<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01855</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9538278a-71a7-4c62-8084-adbd243be166</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">This graph represents the revenue in dollars that a company expects if they sell their product for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> dollars.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The horizontal-axis represents the product price in dollars and the vertical-axis represents the revenue in dollars. The x-axis scale is 2 and extends from 0 to 22. The y-axis scale is 500 and extends from 0 to 6,000.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_09_01.svg" width="324"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>

        <exercise id="_7df5f3e7-792b-4438-a54b-e9a7d2660cd7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00003">Based on this model, which price would generate more revenue for the company, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00004"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, as it would generate about <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>700</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in revenue. Charging <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would bring in about <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
           
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_91a80edb-e118-490e-9da1-3a90f3dac2be" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00006">At what price (in dollars) should the company sell their product if they wish to make as much revenue as possible?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Based on the graph, a price of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would bring in the most revenue.</para>
            <para id="para-00008"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Based on the graph, a price of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would bring in the most revenue.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="dd50d498-c21d-414b-ad51-cdebc7560f33" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00009">How much revenue (in dollars) would they make?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Based on the graph, a price of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would bring in about <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00011"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Based on the graph, a price of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would bring in about <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00012">What is an appropriate domain for the function? Explain how you know.</para>
            <para id="para-00013"></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
            <para id="para-00015"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, because the price has to be non-negative, and the company would earn negative revenue if the price were more than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    
    </section>
  </content>
